It builds against, but does not include, the pcrecomp toolkit (MIT):
https://github.com/sp00nznet/pcrecomp

The DOS machine in src/ comes from the Blake Stone recomp
(https://github.com/sp00nznet/blakestone, MIT, same author), and
src/present_d3d.c's shader from the Gunman Chronicles recomp (MIT, same
author). Nothing in this repository is derived from id Software's source
release of Wolfenstein 3-D (GPL): what the runtime knows about the game was
read out of the shipping executable with the pcrecomp disassembler.

Optional, and not included: the NVIDIA DLSS SDK. tools/get_dlss.py downloads
it into the gitignored external/dlss-sdk/ for your own build, under the NVIDIA
RTX SDKs licence (https://github.com/NVIDIA/DLSS/blob/v310.9.1/LICENSE.txt).
src/dlss.cpp is this project's own code (MIT) that calls it.

Wolfenstein 3-D is commercial software (id Software; published today by
Bethesda/ZeniMax). Neither the game, nor anything generated from its
executable, is part of this repository.
